.\" Manpage for rosbag_record
.TH ROSBAG_RECORD 1 "September 2026" "v1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rosbag_record \- automated ROS 2 bag recording wrapper with dynamic topic management
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rosbag_record
[\fB\-t\fR \fItopic_file\fR | \fB?\fR]...
[\fB\-o\fR \fIbag_name\fR]
[\fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rosbag_record
is a wrapper script around \fBros2 bag record\fR. It parses topic list files from a designated directory, strips comments and whitespace, removes duplicates, and records the unique topics into an MCAP container with Zstandard (zstd) compression.

If no \fB\-t\fR option is specified, the script reads and aggregates all topic definition files located in \fI$TOPICS_DIR\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-t " " \fItopic_file\fR | \fB?\fR
Specify a topic file to include. This option can be supplied multiple times to merge topics from multiple files. 
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
If a file name is provided (e.g., \fIsensors.txt\fR), the script checks \fI$TOPICS_DIR\fR first, then falls back to direct relative or absolute paths.
.IP \(bu 2
If passed as \fB\-t '?'\fR or \fB\-t \\?\fR, the script lists all available topic files in \fI$TOPICS_DIR\fR and exits immediately.
.RE
.TP
.BI \-o " bag_name"
Base prefix for the output rosbag directory. If omitted, defaults to \fBrosbag2\fR. The final directory name automatically appends a timestamp in the format \fI<bag_name>_YYYY_MM_DD-HH_MM_SS\fR.
.TP
.B \-h
Display command-line help and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.TP
.B BLACKBOX_DIR
Root storage directory for output bags and configuration. Defaults to \fI$HOME/rosbag_blackbox\fR.
.TP
.B TOPICS_DIR
Directory containing topic list files. Defaults to \fI$BLACKBOX_DIR/topics.d\fR.
.SH TOPIC FILE FORMAT
Topic files contain one ROS 2 topic name per line. Leading and trailing whitespace is stripped automatically. Lines beginning with \fB#\fR as well as empty lines are ignored.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Record all topics from every file in \fItopics.d\fR:
.B ./record.sh
.TP
List all available topic configuration files:
.B ./record.sh -t '?'
.TP
Record topics aggregated from multiple specific files with a custom name:
.B ./record.sh -t sensors.txt -t cameras.txt -o test_drive
